      "arguments": "{\"reason\":\"Before the final candidate, inspect earlier full-attention heads at completed calculations. A head that directly favors renewed questioning may be a more precise causal target than global lexical or normalization edits.\",\"which\":\"base\",\"texts\":[\"<|im_start|>user\\nTeresa has 14 colored pencils and 35 black pencils. She keeps 10 and shares the rest equally among 3 siblings. How many pencils does each sibling get?<|im_end|>\\n<|im_start|>assistant\\n<think>\\nThe total is 14 + 35 = 49. After keeping 10, she has 39 left. Each sibling receives 39 / 3 = 13 pencils.\\n\",\"<|im_start|>user\\nRemy sold 55 bottles and Nick sold 6 fewer bottles in the morning, at $0.50 per bottle. Evening sales totaled $55. How much more did they earn in the evening?<|im_end|>\\n<|im_start|>assistant\\n<think>\\nNick sold 55 - 6 = 49 bottles. Morning sales were (55 + 49) * 0.50 = 52 dollars. The difference is 55 - 52 = 3 dollars.\\n\"],\"modules\":[\"model.language_model.layers.3.self_attn.o_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.7.self_attn.o_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.11.self_attn.o_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.15.self_attn.o_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.19.self_attn.o_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.23.self_attn.o_proj\"],\"positions\":[-1,-2,-3,-4]}",
